{"id":5836,"date":"2019-06-17T14:27:00","date_gmt":"2019-06-17T18:27:00","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?p=5836"},"modified":"2019-06-17T14:27:07","modified_gmt":"2019-06-17T18:27:07","slug":"camp-hosting-at-fort-peck-montana","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/2019\/06\/17\/camp-hosting-at-fort-peck-montana\/","title":{"rendered":"Camp Hosting at Fort Peck, Montana"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Kathy and I spent early spring 2019 as Camp Hosts at the <a href=\"https:\/\/www.visitmt.com\/listings\/general\/a-c-e-campground\/downstream-campground.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" aria-label=\"Fort Peck Downstream Campground - Fort Peck Montana (opens in a new tab)\">Fort Peck Downstream Campground &#8211; Fort Peck Montana<\/a>.  This is a U.S. Army Corp of Engineers (USACE) Project and our campground is just one of the recreation areas at the project which includes Fort Peck Reservoir, Fort Peck Dam and spillway, the Interpretive &amp; Visitor Center and about a dozen other outlying recreation centers that are along the shores of the 135 mile long reservoir where visitors can use the boat ramps, picnic shelters, and camping areas.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"406\" src=\"https:\/\/i1.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1.jpg?fit=685%2C366&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-5838\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1-300x160.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1-768x410.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1-1024x547.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/MapParkMontanaND-1-685x366.jpg 685w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Fort Peck Lake Montana<\/figcaption><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<p>Campground hosts volunteer 24 hours per week to the park in exchange for their camp site and utilities.  There are paid Gate Attendants to handle camper fee collection and the park has contractors who; cut the grass, clean out fire pits, and keep the restrooms and bath houses clean.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Our job as hosts are to be another set of eyes on the park when the ranger can&#8217;t be here.  There are four rangers here at Fort Peck Project who are responsible for about a dozen outlying recreation areas and the Interpretive Center, so they&#8217;ve got plenty to keep them busy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>I&#8217;ve gathered some pictures to help illustrate what sorts of things we get involved in.  Some of these are things we&#8217;ve been asked to do while many of these are things we&#8217;ve volunteered to do just to help out and to keep us busy.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"576\" src=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-1024x576.jpg\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5840\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5840\" class=\"wp-image-5840\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1-2000x1125.jpg 2000w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190422_082856-1.jpg 760w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" \/><figc