kathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190426_132833-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190426_132833-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190426_132833-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190426_132833-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Have chainsaw, will cut firewood<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i1.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5853\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5853\" class=\"wp-image-5853\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_091324-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Helping Ranger Sue install a dock in the Donut Pond<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5854\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5854\" class=\"wp-image-5854\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190507_095406-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>After installing the dock at the donut pond<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5855\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5855\" class=\"wp-image-5855\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190509_150542-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>We pulled all the utility flags after the comfort station construction was completed<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"760\" height=\"428\" src=\"https:\/\/i2.wp.com\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158.jpg?fit=685%2C385&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"\" data-id=\"5856\" data-link=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/?attachment_id=5856\" class=\"wp-image-5856\" srcset=\"https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158.jpg 760w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158-300x169.jpg 300w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158-768x432.jpg 768w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158-685x385.jpg 685w, https:\/\/herbnkathy.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2019\/05\/20190510_123158-2000x1125.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 760px) 100vw, 760px\" \/><figcaption>Kathy and I prepared the  electric boats to take over to the pond for the field day kids to use<\/figcaption><\/figure><\/li><\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p>There&#8217;s lots to do here, and lots of &#8220;pieces parts&#8221; and equipment to do it with.  The challenge is having enough staff to get it all done before the onslaught of visitors each spring.  That&#8217;s where volunteers can help out.  We can do the &#8220;little jobs&#8221; that might otherwise require time from the (4) rangers and (2) maintenance personnel on staff here at the project.  That way these folks can utilize their time more wisely doing the types of jobs that their specialized training allows them to do.  <\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>One example of the specialized training I mentioned is shown in the photos below.  Last year the campground received a new comfort station.  The staff here at the project performed the complete operation.  They poured the concrete pad for the comfort station to sit on, they did all the trenching and back fill for the supply lines, they did all the rough in plumbing and electrical, they&#8217;ll be doing all the final connections, and they will set forms and pour all the concrete curtain and approach walks.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-gallery columns-3 is-cropped wp-block-gallery-3 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\"><li class=\"blocks-gallery-item\"><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" w